    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "Acts 1:16",
        "textualBasisJa": "“Brothers, it was necessary that this Scripture should be fulfilled, which the Holy Spirit spoke before by the mouth of David concerning Judas, who was guide to those who took Jesus."
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 2:25",
        "textualBasisJa": "For David says concerning him, ‘I saw the Lord always before my face, for he is on my right hand, that I should not be moved."
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 2:29",
        "textualBasisJa": "“Brothers, I may tell you freely of the patriarch David, that he both died and was buried, and his tomb is with us to this day."
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 2:34",
        "textualBasisJa": "For David didn’t ascend into the heavens, but he says himself, ‘The Lord said to my Lord, “Sit by my right hand"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 4:25",
        "textualBasisJa": "who by the mouth of your servant David, said, ‘Why do the nations rage, and the peoples plot a vain thing?"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 7:45",
        "textualBasisJa": "which also our fathers, in their turn, brought in with Joshua when they entered into the possession of the nations whom God drove out before the face of our fathers to the days of David,"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 13:22",
        "textualBasisJa": "When he had removed him, he raised up David to be their king, to whom he also testified, ‘I have found David the son of Jesse, a man after my heart, who will do all my will.’"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 13:34",
        "textualBasisJa": "“Concerning that he raised him up from the dead, now no more to return to corruption, he has spoken thus: ‘I will give you the holy and sure blessings of David.’"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 13:36",
        "textualBasisJa": "For David, after he had in his own generation served the counsel of God, fell asleep, was laid with his fathers, and saw decay."
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 15:16",
        "textualBasisJa": "‘After these things I will return. I will again build the tabernacle of David, which has fallen. I will again build its ruins. I will set it up"
      }
    ],
